cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "faultinject: fault-injection campaigns for GNC and communications software"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-05
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A sixteen-kind fault taxonomy for guidance, navigation, control and
  communications software, with units, declared parameter ranges and a coverage
  binning; injection into a target loop through a wrapper that does not require
  modifying the target; coverage accounting over the taxonomy cross product;
  severity scoring from the target response; bit-identical seeded replay of any
  single case; and a learned campaign prioritiser with an uncertainty output,
  benchmarked on the same budget against uniform-random and coverage-greedy
  search with bootstrap confidence intervals. Validation level 2, research
  grade. Not flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for operational
  aerospace use.
authors:
  - name: "OPTIMA Organisation"
keywords:
  - fault-injection
  - fault-tolerance
  - fdir
  - gnc
  - kalman-filter
  - coverage
  - campaign
  - reproducibility
